# Diagnostic-only environment: print the previous boot's crash log and stop.
#
# This image never boots anything, on purpose. The one thing that tells us why
# Linux died is the console log pstore left in ramoops@e2000000 - and there is
# no other way to get it out of this device: the vendor memory-dump screen
# replaces the whole panel, the board has no UART pads, and the USB gadget is
# unproven on kaanapali. So flash this image, power on, and read the log off
# the screen at your leisure: the screen is static because bootcmd ends in
# `pause`, and md.b prints each line as hex plus an ASCII column - the ASCII
# column on the right is the log.
#
# It is built alongside the normal image (configs/qcom_nx809j_dump_defconfig).
stdin=serial
stdout=vidconsole
stderr=vidconsole

bootcmd=echo; \
echo "=== NX809J crash-log dump (this image never boots anything) ==="; \
echo "--- ramoops@e2000000 zone header: signature / start / size ---"; \
md.b 0xe2000000 0x10; \
echo "--- console log: first 1 KiB of the zone, data starts at 0xe200000c ---"; \
md.b 0xe200000c 0x400; \
echo "--- end of dump. If the log is empty (zeros), the previous boot died"; \
echo "--- before pstore existed, which means something very early.        ---"; \
pause
